{
  "id": "jpGalleryDaily01",
  "name": "Save new job postings from JobsPipe to Google Sheets every day",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "template-description",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1020,
        "content": "## Save new job postings from JobsPipe to Google Sheets every day\n\n### Who's it for\nRecruiters, sales teams tracking hiring signals, job-board builders and researchers who want a daily sheet of fresh job postings without scraping job boards themselves.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every day at 07:00** starts the run.\n2. **Set search filters** holds what to look for: job titles, countries, how far back to look and the page size.\n3. **Search new jobs** calls the JobsPipe API for postings first discovered in the lookback window. JobsPipe collects live postings from 30+ job boards and applicant tracking systems (Workday, Greenhouse, Lever, LinkedIn and more), deduplicated into one schema. The node pages through results with a cursor.\n4. **One item per job** splits the results, and **Add or update rows** writes them to your sheet, matched on `id`, so reruns never duplicate a job.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Get a free API key at jobspipe.dev (1,000 free credits, no card).\n2. In n8n, create a **Header Auth** credential named `JobsPipe API`: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer jp_live_...`. Open **Search new jobs** once so it picks it up.\n3. Edit **Set search filters**.\n4. In **Add or update rows**, connect Google and pick your spreadsheet. Row 1 needs: `id`, `job_title`, `company`, `location`, `url`, `date_posted`, `salary_string`, `min_annual_salary`, `max_annual_salary`, `salary_currency`, `discovered_at`.\n\n### Requirements\n- JobsPipe API key (free tier works)\n- Google account with a spreadsheet\n\n### How to customize\nAdd any filter from docs.jobspipe.dev/api-reference/filters (salary, remote, seniority, company, skills) to the JSON body. Each job costs 1 credit, once per month; this setup reads at most 4 pages of 25 (100 credits) per run. Raise **Max Pages** under the HTTP node's Pagination option for more."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1-sticky",
      "name": "Step 1 sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 1. When and what\nRuns daily at 07:00. Edit job titles, countries, lookback and page size in **Set search filters**. Keep the lookback a little over the schedule interval (25 h for daily) so a late run misses nothing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2-sticky",
      "name": "Step 2 sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        440,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 320,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 2. Fetch from JobsPipe\nPOST /v1/jobs/search with your `JobsPipe API` Header Auth credential. Pagination follows `metadata.next_cursor`, 600 ms apart (Free allows 2 requests/second), max 4 pages."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3-sticky",
      "name": "Step 3 sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        780,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 3. Write to the sheet\nOne row per job, matched on `id`: jobs seen in an overlapping run are updated, not duplicated, and are not charged again that month."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2f504e8a-adcc-521a-a1c8-99aa31f22fbc",
      "name": "Every day at 07:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "set-search-filters",
      "name": "Set search filters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "name": "job_titles",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "=[\"data engineer\", \"analytics engineer\"]"
            },
            {
              "id": "f2",
              "name": "country_codes",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "=[\"US\"]"
            },
            {
              "id": "f3",
              "name": "lookback_hours",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 25
            },
            {
              "id": "f4",
              "name": "page_size",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 25
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "1f51bdcb-6488-5613-8d30-1153ac455a27",
      "name": "Search new jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        540,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.jobspipe.dev/v1/jobs/search",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "pagination": {
            "pagination": {
              "parameters": {
                "parameters": [
                  {
                    "name": "cursor",
                    "type": "body",
                    "value": "={{ $response.body.metadata.next_cursor }}"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "maxRequests": 4,
              "paginationMode": "updateAParameterInEachRequest",
              "requestInterval": 600,
              "limitPagesFetched": true,
              "completeExpression": "={{ !$response.body.metadata.next_cursor }}",
              "paginationCompleteWhen": "other"
            }
          }
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  job_title_or: $json.job_titles,\n  job_country_code_or: $json.country_codes,\n  discovered_at_gte: $now.toUTC().minus({ hours: $json.lookback_hours }).toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss'),\n  limit: $json.page_size\n}) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "JobsPipe API"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "415ddda8-390c-558b-95d6-68cc5704e1d3",
      "name": "One item per job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitOut",
